-- examples/checks/staged-neg-why-data.rofl — a firing staged @next that
-- reads a NEGATION, over a fact that arrives in the very tick it is asked in.
-- q(a) at tick 0: p(a) is staged because r(a) did not hold at tick 0, and
-- r(a) is staged by the same tick, so at tick 1 both hold.
edb(sn_q).
sn_q(a).
-- carried, so the premise is still a record in the tick it is asked in (see f_the_ts_explain_bridge_cannot_name_a_past_premise_that_is_gone)
sn_q(X)@next :- sn_q(X).
sn_p(X)@next :- sn_q(X), not sn_r(X).
sn_r(a)@next :- sn_q(a).
